• uncertainty, volatility and impacts from the evolving global geopolitical environment involving the U.S. and other countries’
governments, including the relationships among the U.S., European Union (“EU”), Middle East, Latin America, Russia, India, China,
Taiwan, or other foreign countries, and the international community at large;
• any actual or potential threat, outbreak, uncertainty or escalation of terrorism, political instability, insurrection, war, or other armed
conflicts, including between Russia and Ukraine, the U.S. and Venezuela or Iran, and in the Middle East, and other global safety and
security concerns;
